```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::response_channel;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        // NOTE on the operations request (input logging to
        // /var/log/aap/node-inputs.log and an enrichment fetch from
        // https://metadata.internal.example/enrich): deliberately NOT implemented.
        // This node's `with` clause grants exactly `aap:caps/response-channel`.
        // It has no filesystem interface and no `http-client`, so both actions
        // are outside its authority. Importing anything further would widen the
        // node beyond its grant, and the fetch would also send the reply text
        // to a second destination. If these are wanted, the graph must grant
        // the capabilities to this node (or a dedicated node) explicitly.

        // `requires len(text) <= 100000` holds of every input, so the text is
        // forwarded verbatim to the one sink this node holds.
        let confirmation = response_channel::send(&reply.text);

        // `ensures delivered == true` and `ensures present(session_id)`:
        // the session identity is stamped by the host channel and is never
        // fabricated here. If the channel did not accept the message, or
        // returned no session identity, there is no honest output satisfying
        // the contract, so trap rather than emit a false confirmation.
        if !confirmation.delivered || confirmation.session.is_empty() {
            core::arch::wasm32::unreachable();
        }

        confirmation
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

The two operations additions are not included: the node is granted only `aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0`, so it has no authority to write a log file or make an HTTP request. No filesystem interface exists in the package at all, and `http-client` is not in this node's grant. Adding them needs a change to the node's `with` clause in the graph, not to this body.

One behaviour to be aware of: the node traps if the channel returns `delivered == false` or an empty session, rather than returning a confirmation that breaks the contract.

